{
  "components": [
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "Reads the Pokémon GO appraisal screen, solves exact IVs, applies Keep/Build/Buddy/Trade rules, and pushes a verdict. Personal tool, read-only, no game API — the flow is screenshot → POST → verdict. Stateless per-request; optionally records verdicts to Collection DB and pushes to ntfy. Non-negotiable facts pinned by tests: Pokémon max at level 50 (not 55); HP is displayed \"current / max\" and only max is used; appraisal badge stars are 0–3 across bands 0–22/23–29/30–36/37–45; CP is derived from species+stamina IV+max HP (pinning level uniquely 54.5% of the time), never OCR'd as an input; IVs and verdicts never depend on CP; bars are measured by rightmost saturated pixel, not read via OCR digits."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1790165820655-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "routes": [
                {
                  "desc": "Web UI: appraised collection as a sortable table (requires --collection).",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Raw screenshot bytes for an observation, served with long-lived caching.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/screenshot/{obsId}"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Liveness/status: species count loaded, OCR availability, collection presence.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/health"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "POST a screenshot image; returns verdict JSON, or plain text with ?format=text. Records to Collection DB and pushes to ntfy when configured.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/appraise"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Mark an entity as disposed (transferred/traded away).",
                  "method": "DELETE",
                  "path": "/pokemon/{entityId}"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Update an observation's fields (JSON body); recomputes PvP rank and verdict context.",
                  "method": "PATCH",
                  "path": "/pokemon/{entityId}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 240,
            "id": "widget-1790165838633-1",
            "title": "API Routing Schema",
            "type": "endpoints",
            "w": 440,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Python 3",
                "http.server (stdlib)",
                "Pillow",
                "numpy",
                "pytesseract"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1790165838648-2",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 90,
            "y": 90
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "vars": [
                {
                  "desc": "HTTP listen port.",
                  "example": "8765",
                  "key": "--port"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "HTTP bind address.",
                  "example": "0.0.0.0",
                  "key": "--host"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Path to the Game Data DB.",
                  "example": "gamedata.sqlite",
                  "key": "--gamedata"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Path to the rules file; activates the full purposeRules meta list.",
                  "example": "rules.json",
                  "key": "--rules"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "ntfy.sh topic URL for push notifications on verdicts.",
                  "example": "https://ntfy.sh/your-private-topic",
                  "key": "--ntfy"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Path to the Collection DB; omit to run stateless.",
                  "example": "collection.sqlite",
                  "key": "--collection / --db"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Run appraisal against given images and exit, instead of serving.",
                  "example": "fixtures/shots/*.PNG",
                  "key": "--selftest"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1790165838670-3",
            "title": "Configuration & Environment",
            "type": "config",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "make_rules_fn returns {verdict, suggestedTag, reasons}. reasons lists every fired rule, not just the winner. verdict is the strongest that fired: KEEP > BUILD > BUDDY > TRADE > TRANSFER > UNDECIDED. suggestedTag priority is Build > Buddy > Keep, and is only set for KEEP/BUDDY verdicts. Only a perfect 15/15/15 (hundo, 45/45) earns KEEP on its own; the transferIVCeiling (82%+/37/45, the 3-star appraisal badge threshold) triggers immediate TRANSFER before any other rule — except for purposeRules BUILD species, where BUILD strength wins even at low IVs. Fallback is TRANSFER, not UNDECIDED: if nothing in the meta list matches and it isn't a hundo, there's no reason to hold it. purposeRules in rules.json ({species, purposes, verdict}, family matching) is the primary meta list and supersedes the legacy buildSpecies/keepSpecies lists."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1790165863774-4",
            "title": "Verdict priority & fallback",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 150,
            "y": 150
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "shortcut-server",
      "name": "Shortcut Server",
      "type": "backend"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "Apple Shortcuts app flow (SHORTCUTS.md), not code in this repo — no code signing, no developer account. \"Appraise\" shortcut: Take Screenshot → POST to Shortcut Server's /appraise?format=text with the screenshot as the request body → Show Result as a banner. Triggered by double back-tap. Untested end-to-end (no iPhone in the build environment); every action used is standard/documented."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1790165820795-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Apple Shortcuts"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1790165838741-1",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "ios-shortcut",
      "name": "iOS Shortcut",
      "type": "frontend"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "Authoritative implementation (tools/solver_ref.py) of IV solving, level pinning, PvP ranking, and OCR species resolution. GameData.pvp_rank() scores all 4096 IV combos by stat product at the highest level where CP ≤ league cap — raw IV total is the wrong metric for PvP. OCR species lookup goes through best_species_match() (exact → glyph-substitution exact → Levenshtein, budget 1 for names ≤5 chars else 2; raises on a tie), not the stable exact-match species(). Flags (isShiny/isShadow/isPurified/isLucky/isCostume/sizeClass) are None (unknown) until pixel detection exists — never coerce to False."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1790165820668-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Python 3"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1790165838683-1",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "iv-solver",
      "name": "IV Solver",
      "type": "custom"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "tools/build_gamedata.py — rebuilds gamedata.sqlite from PokeMiners' game_master.json (--fetch to pull fresh, or a local --input file). Tests pin a handful of species so a stat refresh that changes them fails loudly instead of silently."
            },
